  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $M=8 \\times 10^{22} \\mathrm{Am}^2$\n$$\n\\mathrm{d}=\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{e}}=6.4 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~m}\n$$\nEarth's magnetic field, $\\mathrm{B}=\\frac{\\mu_0}{4 \\pi} \\cdot \\frac{2 \\mathrm{M}}{\\mathrm{d}^3}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\pi} \\times \\frac{2 \\times 8 \\times 10^{22}}{\\left(6.4 \\times 10^6\\right)^3} \\\\\n&\\cong 0.6 \\text { Gauss }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
